.TH FUZZYGENE 1 2000-1月 "fuzzygene_sensitivity" "fuzzygene_sensitivity"
.SH NAME
fuzzygene_sensitivity \- Model self-check: omega invariance, step invariance and lag ordering robustness.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIfuzzygene_sensitivity(\fBfuzzygene\fR as <generic> FuzzyGeneModel, 
\fBgene\fR as string, 
\fBmode\fR as string = "knockout", 
\fBomegas\fR as double = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBstepsList\fR as double = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBsweepSteps\fR as integer = 50, 
\fBreferenceOmega\fR as double = NAN, 
\fBtolerance\fR as double = 0.001, 
\fBlagRatio\fR as double = 0.1, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Model self-check: omega invariance, step invariance and lag ordering robustness.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBfuzzygene\fB \fR\- a trained (or restored) model. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgene\fB \fR\- the target gene of the virtual perturbation. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmode\fB \fR\- \fBknockout\fR (default), \fBknockdown\fR or \fBoverexpression\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBomegas\fB \fR\- relaxation values to sweep, e.g. \fBc(0.2, 0.5, 0.8, 1.0)\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBstepsList\fB \fR\- iteration budgets to sweep, e.g. \fBc(50, 200, 500)\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBsweepSteps\fB \fR\- fixed iteration budget used by the omega sweep and the lag analysis. 
.PP
.PP
\fBreferenceOmega\fB \fR\- omega used as the comparison baseline; \fBNaN\fR picks the value closest to 0.5. 
.PP
.PP
\fBtolerance\fB \fR\- relative deviation threshold of the invariant flags. 
.PP
.PP
\fBlagRatio\fB \fR\- relative trigger threshold of the lag definition. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment used to report errors. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a named list of data.frames
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
Returns a named list:
 


 
- \fBomega\fR: data.frame \fBvalue\fR / \fBconverged\fR / \fBiterations\fR /
 \fBlast_max_delta\fR / \fBmax_abs_deviation\fR / \fBmax_relative_deviation\fR; the deviation
 columns are measured against \fBreference_omega\fR (see \fBsummary\fR);
- \fBsteps\fR: the same shape for the iteration budget sweep, measured
 against the largest step count;
- \fBlag\fR: wide table \fBgene\fR + one column per omega, each cell is the
 frame index at which that gene first reaches 10% (\fBlagRatio\fR) of its own final change;
- \fBspearman\fR: wide table of pairwise Spearman rho between the omega runs,
 computed on the genes that respond under every omega;
- \fBsummary\fR: one row data.frame with the two invariant flags, the
 reference values, the responding gene count, the mean rho and the run count.


 


 Read \fBsummary$omega_invariant\fR first. \fBFALSE\fR means the end state still depends on the
 damping factor, i.e. the iteration has not converged and the trajectory is not a steady
 state. That is a property of the model, not a bug of this function.
 


 


 Cost: about \fB2 x (length(omegas) + length(stepsList) + length(omegas))\fR solves. With the
 default grids on an 18k gene model this takes roughly one minute.
.PP
